# Version honesty

## Stable installs

Pin user-facing install examples to the **latest stable tag** (`v2.6.0` as of 18 Nov 2026):

- Docker: `prest/prest:v2.6.0`
- Go: `go install github.com/prest/prest/v2/cmd/prestd@v2.6.0`

Do not leave install paths on older stable tags while hubs advertise a newer release.

Feature gates can still say “v2.1.0+” (MCP), “v2.2.0+” (Studio, database-backed queries), “v2.4.0+” (OpenTelemetry, pgvector KNN/distance filtering), “v2.4.1+” (MCP honours `[expose]`), “v2.4.2+” (HMAC `jwt.key` minimums, `jwt.algo` enforcement, `sqlVal`/`sqlList`/`ident` binding, SQL removed from logs), “v2.5.0+” (MySQL `engine = "mysql"`, JOIN ACL under `restrict`, middleware plugin builds), “v2.5.1+” (MySQL MCP, registry `{schema}` scope, and the type/503/batch fixes), “v2.5.2+” (reserved `prest_users`/`prest_queries` tables, catalog/`/show`/`/_PLUGIN` behind auth, plugin name rules, `pg.allowed_databases`, `pg.single` removed), “v2.5.3+” (unfiltered `DELETE`/`PUT`/`PATCH` refused, `access.allow_unscoped_writes`, `fields` enforced on writes and on every column a read references), or “v2.6.0+” (request IDs `http.request_id_header`, `pg.application_name`, MCP `protocolVersion` negotiation, `PREST_CONFIG_JSON`, `http.allowed_hosts`, `pg.timezone`, `auth.token_ttl`, `prestd auth create-user`, `$contains` on array columns, rows/columns/msgpack renderers) when describing when a feature landed.

## Unreleased `main`

Features only on `prest/prest` main (not yet tagged) must be labeled:

- `{% hint style="warning" %}` **Requires prest `main` (unreleased)** + PR link
- Never claim they ship in a tag they are not on

Claim upgrade/install steps only for tagged releases. See `write-docs` voice do-not-claim.
